{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1469515-1001-mummy-2e-plot-hooks","id":1469515,"title":"1001 Mummy 2e Plot Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-03T12:16:57-08:00","id":1469515,"title":"1001 Mummy 2e Plot Hooks","content":"Thought I'd start a new MtC 1001 Plot Hooks thread.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The meret awakens to find themselves inside a museum exhibit, during business hours and at least a dozen witnesses.</li> <li>The meret uncovers a medical company draining a dormant mummy for their &quot;stem cells&quot;. The company is a front for the mummy's cult, but there is no proof they would have consented to such treatment.</li> <li>A vampire with memories of Irem has been openly talking about it to others. Clearly the vampire has been feeding off of an Arisen, but the question is who and why did they leave the vampire alive?</li> <li>A mummy who has lost their cult and found true love during an Auspicious Descent comes to the meret to help save their love from a grizzly fate.</li> <li>A Relic is being used as a prop for a musician's concert tour.</li> <li>An Immortal has taken a position in the FBI with the strict purpose of &quot;deprogramming&quot; the meret's cult.</li> <li>An abandoned tomb is uncovered within the city, the cult was destroyed decades prior, but the arisen still lays there dormant. But their Relics are unprotected.</li> <li>A police raid on a drug ring lead to the death of dozens of drug dealers and officers, but also a mummified corpse was discovered in the center of the carnage. The truth is likely that the drug ring was an Arisen's Cult and the Arisen's corpse has been taken to the city morgue.</li> <li>Reports of a chimeric monster running amok in the city park has caused cryptozoologists to flock to the city. An Amkhata is likely the cause.</li> <li>An expert team of thieves have robbed the meret's Tombs while they were distracted. A hunter and their crew has claimed responsibility and will return the Relics and Canopic Jars as well as additional Relics they've previously uncovered in exchange for assistance in dealing with a great threat.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T15:40:59-08:00","id":1469535,"title":"","content":"11. Arisen encounters an Immortal under good terms, but a memory is triggered showing that in a future they will turn traitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T06:30:45-08:00","id":1469573,"title":"","content":"12. The meret have been accused by another of their kind of a grave crime in a prior Descent, but they do not remember it at all. How can they gather evidence to mount a defense when they have no memory of the incident - and what happens if it turns out they are guilty after all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-04-2021, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T06:39:18-08:00","id":1469574,"title":"","content":"13. Arisen have been going missing, and the meret eventually trace the disappearances back to one of their own kind, an unscrupulous Alchemist whose cult have devised a form of the Exudation ritual which allows the Sekhem of one mummy to be drained to feed another's soul. The Alchemist sees this substance as the ultimate manifestation of Dedwen, and seeks to use it to become truly immortal and achieve Apotheosis in this Descent, before they must face the Judges once more. Can the meret bring this blasphemy to an end, and if they can (or if they join the heretic) what will they do with their blasphemous research?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T06:43:26-08:00","id":1469575,"title":"","content":"14. The meret awaken and are tasked by the Judges with hunting down a certain Vessel, as is normal. When they discover it, however, the man in possession of it claims to be a sorcerer, and offers his services in making more Vessels in exchange for his life. Do the Judges wish this man slain out of hand or for his bargain to be accepted, and if the meret do accept, what lengths will they go to to defend their new treasure from others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T14:36:13-08:00","id":1469665,"title":"","content":"15. The immortals known as the Purified are a frustrating mystery to the Arisen and yet paradoxically one of the oldest groups of undying individuals known to the Deathless. Their form of immortality is as close as any to the Arisen's own Rite of Return as the mummies have ever witnessed, and indeed one method of Purification may be based directly on the mummy's own rituals (both the Outer Path of Purification and the Rite of Return originate in the Nile Delta, and both claim to be the secret inspiration behind the Ancient Egyptian obsession with mundane mummification). This faction of Purified often allied with the Arisen in the earliest days, and some Mummies even assisted in granting their servants this form of immortality when other options were unavailable (specifically, it was seen as a fine substitute for a Sadikh when another servant had already been granted that boon). But some Mummies began to compare Purification with the mummy heresy known as Apotheosis, a similar quest to enlighten the soul of a Deathless and break the need to return to Duat and serve the Judges. That decree is ancient and mostly forgotten, but some of mummies that serve the Shepherds recall the mandate and have risen to hunt local Purified in the Nome of the meret. Which side do the Arisen choose?<br /> <br /> 16. There are other forms of Purification. Perhaps the largest faction of Purified in the world comes from ancient Chinese taoist traditions, stemming from alchemists seeking to imbue their spirit with purfied chi and their flesh with unending life. Chinese history in the real world is filled with numerous historical examples of Dynastic Emperors obsessed with achieving this same divine state by any means necessary, and there are no doubt still more crueler and darker examples of this in the history of the Chronicles. Unfortunately, the Arisen are entangled in this ancient history as well, and not always in the most flattering of ways. The Alchemists Guild especially was fascinated by the far Eastern examples of their ancient arts and through various means and proxies often partnered with Emperors and nobles of the various dynasties of China to learn more. However, as is the way of that guild, the Arisen just as often offered lies and half truths as genuine promises of an immortality serum, and even the most well intentioned of Mummies often failed to create an effective elixir of life (and to be fair, this method of Purification has never been completely reliable even to the most learned of sages). Very unfortunate indeed, because Chinese emperors were never very forgiving of failure as a general rule, and their burial practices tended to involve vast tombs, immense offerings and charms to aid them in the afterlife, and occasionally large numbers of deceased servants or whole armies of Effigies to call upon. If a high chinese official lingered on as a ghost, he would be virtually guaranteed to remain as such for thousands of years armed with innumerable Anchors and loyal servants. And an eternal vendetta against the traitors from the western deserts.<br /> <br /> 17. On the other hand, many Purified succeeded, and at least some of them were indeed ancient rulers of China. Given the nature of the Shadow as a reflection of the real world, any former Emperor who mastered immortality and gained access to the other side would be treated precisely there as he was in the real world, albeit with servants and court officials of a much more alien nature. In time, as his power grew he would assimilate into the Shadow's hierarchy and become a spirit unto himself. This would seem to be a great boon to any mummy lucky enough to assist said Emperor in achieving their goal, and in some ways it is. However, is it truly an advantage when a powerful, godlike immortal with a mind either completely alien or dangerously mad comes calling at the gates of your tomb eager to repay their ancient debts? Especially when their &quot;gifts&quot; cause a tide of blood and slaughter across the Nome? And what will the jealous Gods of Duat think of this self-proclaimed Emperor of Heaven usurping the time and loyalty of their chosen servants? For that matter, any Purified this powerful no doubts has many rival spirits and perhaps even other Purified as enemies, and they will be more than happy to drag the Arisen into their alien intrigues.<br /> <br /> 18. He calls himself Dr. Theseus, a wry reference to the Ship of Theseus thought experiment that asks if a vessel that has plied the seas for a long time and been repaired and upgraded so long that none of her timbers are from her original hull can that ship be considered the same one as the original? Theseus likes this question since he himself is almost entirely not made up of his original parts. Theseus is a man who has survived the past 170 years living off the organs and limbs of other people, a hodge podge immortal called a Patchwork Person. The key to his existence is a ticking mechanical devices that keeps his heart beating, running on something more esoteric than electricity (which, given the relationship established between immortals and mummies in the Second Edition, we can safely assume to be Sekhem). The trouble is, his body is constantly breaking down. Every few years another organ needs replacing or another surgery must be performed. Theseus is tired of being in the constant debt of sorcerers and would be Frankensteins just to stay alive. And he has found a solution! While researching the esoteric alchemies that fuel his strange device, Theseus learned of the Arisen and has obtained enough of their secrets to be very, very dangerous. What he finds particularly interesting is the way this ancient rite of return seems to have crafted the immortal's body into a vessel purpose built to contain the flow of Sekhem. Oh yes....and of course, that same function was extended to the organs the ritualists removed from the body and placed in the Canopic Jars. Ancient organs...crafted of impossibly potent magic to stay eternally preserved until the kiss of Sekhem brings them back to life and allows them to work again like new. Theseus already has deep connections to the illicit organ trade. He's even performed a few murders and improptu surgeries on occasion in the name of staying alive. What's a little grave robbing added to the list? The character's canopic jars have become the target of this obsessed man, who intends for his next four surgeries to be his last. He believes that should he replace his current organs with the counterparts of an Arisen's canopic jars that they will make him truly immortal, incorruptible vessels of Sekhem that will never wear out or need replacement. The truth of the matter is whatever the Storyteller likes- they may well simply fail to function completely as one might expect with implanting a long dead organ into a living body. They might make Theseus a unwitting candidate to be a Mummies next body (and if he successfully implants two organs from separate Arisen? Then the lucky doctor might have two ancient, angry souls contesting for his body at the same time!). Perhaps he truly becomes an immortal who will live eternally without need of surgery. If his target turns out to be Deceived, the doctor may even provide the unwitting means for the Shan'iatu to pull their disparate psyches back together in a single body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","user":"nothri","date":". 12-24-2021, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T08:24:33-08:00","id":1469839,"title":"","content":"19. The Arisen has been dealing with at least two other cults that are trying to stop them. As Memory starts to come back to them, they remember forming one of the cults in order to stop themself from doing something really really bad. Could the other cults have been sent by themself in the past as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T11:43:39-08:00","id":1469858,"title":"","content":"20. An Arisen runs into an Immortal who accosts them for an overdue rent payment. Ends up in a previous descent the Arisen had rented a room for a couple months, but returned to Duat before paying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T13:13:07-08:00","id":1471207,"title":"","content":"21. This Descent has been particularly difficult on the Mummy. All Arisen must contend to one degree or another with the new era, whether their last Calling was performed a few years, decades, centuries or millennia ago. But the modern world is particularly unforgiving of those ignorant of science and technology. And yet this world has tempting tools available for those willing to master them. This &quot;smart phone&quot; the Arisen's cultists have presented him with has the power to send missives or speak directly to his followers over any distance, guide him through a city as if he were following an expert guide, and even provide instant access to history new and ancient he might require to better achieve the Purpose he has been summoned to fulfill. And yet mastery does not come easily. Just the other day he found himself entering a bleak, bizarre corner of this 'internet', a website filled with strange images mundane and bizarre that he was utterly unable to extricate his device from. He had to ask for assistance from one of his cult, like a child needing his parent to assist in the mess that he had created. The cultist was of course respectful (and to be fair, not suicidal enough) to show his contempt for the shameful incident, but ever since the mummy has sensed a change in his manner. The old creature has lost face among his followers. In his shame he has not drawn any attention to the strange events that have been taking place around him, fearing it is only his imagination. The cryptic messages and phone calls warning him that &quot;they&quot; are coming and not to let &quot;them&quot; inside. The feeling of being watched, of strange distorted faces appearing in computer monitors and TV screens, there and then with a flicker gone. The increasing interest his cultists seem to take in their devices, staring into their phones without typing or speaking...or the habit they seem to have developed of gathering late at night to watch the TV's static. The mummy has always been a somewhat anachronistic, even technophobic entity, but in this particular era it cannot help but think that technology is actively hunting him, however paranoid that may sound.<br /> <br /> Indeed, as the saying goes just because you are paranoid does not mean they aren't out to get you. In this case, &quot;they&quot; are a group of accidental body thieves trapped within a sinister website dubbed &quot;Death.com&quot; by those aware of its existence. The full details of this modern form of mind swapping can be found in World of Darkness: Immortals. In brief, the website (whose origins are unknown) displays memories from the minds it draws into itself like any normal streaming service. Spend enough time online and the website draws your mind and soul into the site, where it soon becomes enveloped and perhaps even consumed by the thoughts and feelings of all the others that make up the mental network. Occasionally a mind so trapped can escape back into a new body when the site ensnares a new soul. Even more rarely, sometimes something utterly inhuman escapes instead. Other than this, the website is usually content to be a venus flytrap, drawing in minds that come to it. But the mummy is far more tightly bound to its body than the website can affect, and yet burns far more brightly with Sekhem. The souls of Death.com have therefore become rather more...interested. The mummy has drawn their collective attention like moths are drawn to a flame. But being a conglomeration of minds, many completely insane or bound to a dream like fugue, the response of the website has not been very coherent. Many of the souls are victims, and all desire release. Thus it has sought to both warn the mummy against the dangers of the website (hence the cryptic texts and phone calls) and use the Arisen as a means to escape. It has slowly been insinuating itself into the ranks of the mummy's cult, allowing the most loyal souls access to the first pick amongst the cult (&quot;loyal&quot; meaning minds that are willing and able to access the website again and again and showing it to uncorrupted members of the cult, helping to free their brothers). This scenario can be used to maximize the feelings of anachronism and culture shock a mummy is struggling with upon awakening. In addition, the Arisen must ultimately decide whether to allow the currents inhabitants of his former servants keep their bodies (they are as much victims of this horror of modern technology as anyone else) and what to do about his loyal followers now trapped inside the void of the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","user":"nothri","date":". 12-24-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T15:39:44-08:00","id":1471212,"title":"","content":"22. The High priest's kid has summoned you up to deal with their bullies. Adulting mixed in with cosmic horror ensues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T18:04:02-08:00","id":1471220,"title":"","content":"23: You have been awakened by your own cultists violating your tomb, breaking the sacred geometry and even attempting to throw away Vestiges! It appears some kind of sorcerer has taken over your cult in your absence and they seem ignorant of your kind and Vestiges in general, dismissing them as superstitions.They have demanded access to the Rites your cult has learned and obsessively studied &amp; observed the ones your High Priest has performed. This interloper is trying to steal your secrets as well as your followers.<br /> (Mage crossover intended, but could just be a straight Sorcerer)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T20:02:57-08:00","id":1471225,"title":"","content":"24. You awaken after centuries since your last wake\u2026 or you think you did. Looks like you just lost your memory of what you did in the last century, because your High Priest (who\u2019s also your Sadikh), who can\u2019t be <i>that</i> old since she\u2019s your previous High Priest\u2019s granddaughter, claims to be your lover. She doesn\u2019t seem to be lying, too.<br /> While still trying to grasp at why in Duat were you dating your own cultist, a fair lady with pure skin that yet reeks with the smell of blood barges in, claiming that <i>she\u2019s</i> your lover.<br /> A few hours later you meet a \u2018man\u2019 whose body is not her own. Again, she claims to be your lover.<br /> A day or two later, a high-society gentlewoman contacts you, whose life is stored in a ring. She says it\u2019s her and your engagement ring.<br /> In the name of the Judges, just what was happening with your romantic life, with all these endless appearances of Endless lovers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Details. 12-25-2021, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T20:00:24-08:00","id":1471257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1469515-1001-mummy-2e-plot-hooks?p=1471212#post1471212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">22. The High priest's kid has summoned you up to deal with their bullies. Adulting mixed in with cosmic horror ensues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So sort of Lot 249 in reverse perspective? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5A89sKeMGM&amp;ab_channel=SherlockHolmesStoriesMagpieAudio\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5A89sKeMGM&amp;ab_channel=SherlockHolmesStoriesMagpieAudio\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5A89sKeMGM&amp;ab_channel=SherlockHolmesStoriesMagpieAudio </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5A89sKeMGM&amp;ab_channel=SherlockHolmesStoriesMagpieAudio\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5A89sKeMGM&amp;ab_channel=SherlockHolmesStoriesMagpieAudio </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T00:44:26-08:00","id":1471261,"title":"","content":"25: Demonically possessed Lifeless have struck at your cult. You have encountered the unpossessed variant of these blood drinkers before. Reaching out them reveals that normally the tactics these demon-touched blood drinkers are normally applied against them. They have never heard of this &quot;VII&quot; targeting non vampires. But the worst part is that you weren't summoned back to defend your cult. You sent back by your Judge to reclaim the &quot;Old City of your Empire&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T20:40:49-08:00","id":1472926,"title":"","content":"26. The renowned Islamic scholar and Egyptologist of the 14th century, <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Al Maqrizi, once claimed that there was an annual tradition of virgin sacrifice along the Nile to mark the beginning of the flood season. He attributed this practice to the worship of Hapi, a god of the yearly inundation of the Nile and a general lord of fertility and renewal. Modern scholars dispute the existence of these Brides of the Nile (Arous El Nil). But in the Chronicles of Darkness such a grim ritual indeed exists. The Arous El Nil are in fact one of the larger scorpion cults in service to Qerrti, the Double Nile Source. His mandate is to punish those that engage in sexual deviance and perversion. What might offend the bronze age sensibilities of a cosmic horror is anyone's guess. However, the Arous El Nil concern themselves with the inverse of the sins their god punishes, considering virginity sacred and pure and therefore having divine power. Qerrti's name is quite literal- the Iremites like the Egyptians that followed them considered the island of Elephantine near the first cataract of the Nile to be the divine source of the river (the &quot;double nile&quot; refers to the northern and southern portions of Egypt) and believed that the waters flowed up from the underworld through caverns hidden beneath the water. The annual floods came about when Qerrti opened the doors to these hidden chambers and loosed the vital waters upon the land. The Brides were drowned in the river at the start of each year to ensure his favor. The cult still observes that sacrifice in the modern age. According to their own texts, offering a tainted sacrifice or failing to perform the ritual at the appointed hour would result in drought or in a savage flood that would drown whole cities. It is also worth noting that Arous El Nil is a vast cult that does not confines its activities to the Nile Valley alone. The Nile is the mother of all rivers, and the Double Nile Source holds dominion over all great waters. There are sects devoted to his worship along the Amazon, the Yangtze, The Mississippi, the Ganges, the Elbe and a thousand other waters across the continents. Many of them sacrifice their own followers, but many also are content to kidnap children for the ritual as well.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T20:32:41-08:00","id":1475435,"title":"","content":"27. Some fool has finally done it; the Heart of Re has been claimed and actually used. Hundreds of Arisen and thousands of Shuankhsen simultaneously rise and join those who few who were already awake- now empowered by the Cosmic Seba. The world is plunged into a period of chaos for several years, the elongated Descents and the nearly god-like hordes of Bane Mummies scouring the earth like ravenous locusts change the supernatural landscape of the world forever.. nearly exposing the entirety of the World of Darkness to humanity.<br /> <br /> And while this madness reigns, the Deceived quietly, tirelessly search for and bring many hundreds of confused, panicked immortals into the fold; for the Heart of Re has also brought many of their lost brothers and sisters back from their seemingly eternal slumber.. massively increasing their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T17:51:01-08:00","id":1475475,"title":"","content":"28. A mummy has awakened with a terrifying recollection. One of his Descents in the far future reveals that there is indeed other intelligent life in the cosmos, and one of these alien civilizations bears heraldry that is identical to the iconography utilized by the Nameless Empire.<br /> <br /> A few days after this chilling revelation was shared throughout the Nome, said Arisen, his cult, and the entire warehouse that hid the entrance to his Tomb have all vanished, the only thing left behind being a huge scorch mark upon the earth- when viewed from above it is revealed to be in the shape of a gigantic scorpion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T19:20:50-07:00","id":1478316,"title":"","content":"29. People all over the county are falling deathly ill seemingly overnight, and already several have been claimed by this mystery sickness, their bodies consumed by bizarrely rapid cancerous growths: their final moments filled with agony and hysteria. What\u2019s even more disquieting is the sensation of corrupt Sekhem thrumming within the bodies of these victims, powerful enough to be detected through Khepher... and once that\u2019s determined it then becomes horrifyingly apparent that this pervasive wrongness can be felt flowing through water pipes all over the city. <br /> <br /> This toxic metaphysical effluence seems to originating somewhere up north, but the only thing of note in that direction is an artificial reservoir that provides water to all the surrounding towns...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-08-2022, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T18:45:59-07:00","id":1484319,"title":"","content":"30. Out of the blue one night, an ally of the meret's tomb gets attacked by a mysterious Amkhat, utterly ravaging the mummy's place of rest and trashing several vessels before bizarrely absconding with the heavily wounded mummy and leaving only one survivor- the mummy's Sadikh. This begins a city wide chase to find and rescue the kidnapped Arisen, leading to several brutal running battles with the lesser Amkhata that the kidnapping beast has taken as its pack before finally cornering and confronting the abomination. <br /> <br /> But just before the final showdown can begin, the Sphinx-headed monster reveals that it is a creation of one of the meret's members, born several decades ago in order to follow their ally and discover proof of the man's intentions of treachery- this attack was due to it finally witnessing the meret's friend finalizing their plans of betrayal. The supposed creator currently lacks the Memory to recall if they indeed are responsible for creating the beast..leading to a highly uncomfortable dilemma on the groups hands, not knowing who-or what to trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 06-22-2022, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T09:06:49-07:00","id":1487388,"title":"","content":"31)The ruins of Troy have recently become of interest to the Arisen, as recently found during a dig was a small chamber filled with relics and vestiges of Iremite origin! Unfortunately, a unit of Ancient Greek ghosts who claim to be made from dragon\u2019s teeth scattered on the bare earth protect these items from any and all supernatural interlopers. Showing signs of having mutated after being near so much Sekhem for so long, these strange ghosts are only moderately human-looking, now.<br /> <br /> 32)A mummified dog, found in the collection of a reclusive Texas billionaire, has been discovered by the mummy\u2019s cult to be a relic! An uter of great power, this ancient corpse is wrapped in bandages on which Egyptian hieroglyphs honor the dog as an incarnation of Anubis (<i>not</i> Anpu, but the Egyptian version of the god). What does the relic do? Too bad the Texas billionaire is a major customer of Last Dynasty International...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T10:01:39-07:00","id":1487397,"title":"","content":"I like this one. It has a very \u201ccomedy of errors\u201d feel to it!<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1469515-1001-mummy-2e-plot-hooks?p=1471225#post1471225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">24. You awaken after centuries since your last wake\u2026 or you think you did. Looks like you just lost your memory of what you did in the last century, because your High Priest (who\u2019s also your Sadikh), who can\u2019t be <i>that</i> old since she\u2019s your previous High Priest\u2019s granddaughter, claims to be your lover. She doesn\u2019t seem to be lying, too.<br /> While still trying to grasp at why in Duat were you dating your own cultist, a fair lady with pure skin that yet reeks with the smell of blood barges in, claiming that <i>she\u2019s</i> your lover.<br /> A few hours later you meet a \u2018man\u2019 whose body is not her own. Again, she claims to be your lover.<br /> A day or two later, a high-society gentlewoman contacts you, whose life is stored in a ring. She says it\u2019s her and your engagement ring.<br /> In the name of the Judges, just what was happening with your romantic life, with all these endless appearances of Endless lovers?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T19:25:25-07:00","id":1487434,"title":"","content":"33)A cadre of Stone Guardians has been found\u2014-by mortals! Merets around the world scramble to grab these ancient Deathless servants...and so, too, do the Shuankhsen, who seek to turn a member of this minor Guild into a loyal slave of Ammut.<br /> <br /> 34)A major Hollywood actor has joined a cult of the meret\u2019s. They use their influence quite smoothly on the meret\u2019s behalf. <br /> <br /> Then, the actor\u2019s connection to the Cult is exposed by paparazzi! They even publish photos of a (thankfully non-magical!) ceremony being performed!<br /> <br /> Now, the meret\u2019s cult is being bombarded with phone calls, emails and even visits in person to answer questions about the cult, it\u2019s beliefs, it\u2019s goals...and it\u2019s leadership.<br /> <br /> Wat do?<br /> <br /> 35)[Deceived, only]A NASA space satellite falls to earth, and washes ashore somewhere in the Third World, where a Deceived\u2019s cultists piles it into their pickup truck and bring it back with them to town.<br /> <br /> But...it\u2019s a <i>pair</i> of relics: a piece of Neithian architecture, as well as a seba recorded in the satellite\u2019s memory banks. The seba, radio-static insanity sent from the star Vega, contains a strange power: by unleashing it, a dying human being can be transformed into a shapeshifting avian horror!<br /> <br /> The PCs find out about this seba. They want it. Time for a cult war!<br /> <br /> [Yet again, thanksbto Mr. Chris Allen for his Lyrebirds!]<br /> <br /> 36)[Deceived, only]A Storm Lords-only werewolf pack has decided the Deceived are simply a more powerful version of a Claimed. It\u2019s pack vs cult!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-23-2022, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T19:13:33-07:00","id":1487827,"title":"","content":"37)A Slaughterer has escaped from Duat, and has Claimed a young woman who works at some low-paying job. The demon inside her motives her to become a serial killer. She then goes on, still Claimed by the Slaughterer, to become a prolific serial killer. As she can manifest her possessor\u2019s physical traits and the Slaughterer is male, the police have no idea who to look for, wasti g their time on male suspects.<br /> <br /> Due to Sybaritic Omens, a PC discovers the Slaughterer hitched a ride out of Duat with <i>them</i>. Will they fix this grave even, or turn away in indolent absence of empathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:06:26-07:00","id":1487917,"title":"","content":"38)In the rural fields of Wyoming, a horror stalks the farmlands: an undead bear, this monstrosity feeds on farm animals, not to sustain itself, but simply because that is its nature.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it\u2019s also a five-dot Uter relic. The PCs\u2019 meret\u2019s becomes aware of this unusual vessel. Wat do?<br /> <br /> 39)The meret finds itself jumping <i>together</i> through time, specifically going from the 21st Century CE to the first Sothic Turn. Sybaritic Omens slowly point the location of a scroll Text relic that, when properly deciphered, reveals the location of six dormant sha, each sha with an Utterance never before seen.<br /> <br /> This a treasure beyond reckoning, and it appears the Judges are pointing the meret at it, directly.<br /> <br /> 40)A mummy jumps farther into the future than <i>any</i> Arisen thought possible, and discovers millions of years from now the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1431795-apotropaic-mysteries?p=1435140#post1435140\">Karkinos</a> still have merets\u2014-albeit highly <i>alien</i> . How does the PC react to this <i>insanely</i> strange world?<br /> <br /> Many thanks to Professor Phobos for this insanely wonderful creature concept. While the adventure idea in my creation, the Karkinos are purely the doing of Professor Phobos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-25-2022, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T15:06:12-07:00","id":1488602,"title":"","content":"41)A mummy meret becomes convinced a sarira is a relic. The mages guarding the Artifact are <i>not</i> happy having godlike necromancer-immortals breathing down their necks. Meanwhile, a Tremere infiltrator to the consilium has decided to see what a <i>Deathless</i> soul tastes like...<br /> <br /> 42)Somehow, the wine of Shezmu has appeared in extremely specific locations. Madmen claim delirium fever guided them in the brewing and are terrified of gnashing teeth and crushing feet. But wine meant for gods is not meant for lessers, and those who drink the brew descend into absolute madness.<br /> <br /> 43)[Deceived, only]The Star Pharaoh, a Deceived who worships entities from a realm no other Arisen has even heard of, is on the prowl. He seeks a seba that will allow him to visit this strange alien realm of blackness and freezing night, but the temakh of the other Deceived send howling screams into the ears of the Deceived, raving of Ki-En-Gir magics and how this must not come to pass.<br /> <br /> 44)Nothing burns as brightly as eternal love, and nothing hurts as much as love betrayed. You were in love with another Arisen, but one of you\u2014-you\u2019re not sure WHO\u2014-betrayed the other. With every Descent you find each other, and, as Memory increases, it all comes apart. Can this loop of love-become-hate ever be ended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-31-2022, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T14:00:03-07:00","id":1489010,"title":"","content":"45: [Mesen-Nebu focused] Vestiges, while vessels that must be collected, are generally of lesser interest and importance than Relics to the Arisen. However several such Vestiges have arrived lately, with minor odd abilities in addition to those infused with Sekhem. It stirs the memories of the Mesen-Nebu who recall old alchemical secrets. Worse upon further inspection, these Vestiges are the work of a single sorcerer. Are they on the verge of rediscovering alchemical Relic creation, and if so how will the Judges react?<br /> (Inspired by Signs of Sorcery M:tAw and how there is no need to be a willworker to create &quot;Perfected&quot; materials)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T23:38:19-07:00","id":1489062,"title":"","content":"46) Your entire meret is summoned by a bunch of visibly embarrassed looking cultists of all-ages... and the ectoplasmic figures of two slightly-post-Iremite sorcerers throwing dagger-eyes at each other. Turns out these two ancestors have sworn their descendants would carry on their eternal enmity, for all eternity ... but the grudge dates from several centuries now: nobody wants neighborly curses in this economy, there's been plenty of dating and family mixing between the two branches, and the annual day of &quot;<i>summital battle of guile, gore and maddening geometries</i>&quot; stipulated by the two original nemesis has become nothing more than a quiet picnic day between the once rival families.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how it was... before the two ghosts came back, more potent and pissed than ever. And since none of the living had the courage to admit that they dropped the feud (dead wizards ghosts can still pack a mean curse), the specters pretty much bullied them into throwing their biggest assets in the fight: the Deathless guardians of their respective lines... a.k.a, y'all.<br /> <br /> Good luck convincing the angry ghostly patriarchs that the giggling, super-soaker wielding 6-years old are actually engaged in a cutthroat battle, or that the baking contest is actually a thinly veiled clash of sorcerous recipes. Unless you actually decide to unleash your wildest abilities to force the two family to fight together: maybe that would convince the two stooges...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-07-2022, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T21:41:41-07:00","id":1489298,"title":"","content":"47. To Arisen eyes civilization often seems little more than stalks of grain awaiting the harvest, springing forth with each inundation of the Nile only to wither away as the river ebbs, only for the seeds of the fallen society to give birth to a new crop when the cycle repeats. But great empires still earn the respect and attention of the Deathless. The Merovingians and the Carolingian Empire that followed them are one such example, their reputations somewhat bolstered by the number of Arisen active in Europe during their rise and golden age thanks to the Third Sothic Turn. One myth among many born from the Germanic and Norse societies from which they came concerns the hero Sigurd (or Siegfried), a folk hero slayed a dragon and laid claim to an empire only to be betrayed and murdered in a tragic epics that has many variations and inspired many modern works. Some speculate this legendary figure was inspired by Sigebert the first of the Merovingians, although many elements of the story are clearly embellished and mythologized with fantastical elements. Certainly there is no way that Sigebert might have fought a dragon, in the process soaking in the creature's blood, and from this earning an invulnerability similar to the tale of Achilles (and later, like the greek hero, meeting his death from an enemy who exploited a weak spot in that invincibility). <br /> <br /> Or perhaps not. The mummies are awakened to deal with a dire threat. A particularly large and deadly Amkhata has been threatening the region. Yet to their astonishment, the beast is killed before they can arrive. Making inquiries will lead the Deathless to an obscure, ancient sanctuary within the heart of Europe and to a clan of blood bathers who claim to be descended from a line of kings over a thousand years old. According to their own account the bloodbathers were those blessed by members of the family and taught a sacred right of bathing in the fluids of ravening monsters as well as mortal members of their line. So they have survived, immortal and impervious, having had the foresight to devote their familial riches in ancient times to building secluded sanctuaries for themselves against the day their lineages would fall. A grandiose pedigree, assuming it is the truth. In any case, the mummies will have to decide what to do with a group of inbred, highly decadent and certifiably insane immortals who defy the straight forward methods of physical destruction both mundane and supernatural. And if there is one isolated group that survives by invoking this highly potent form of the bathing ritual, there could be others scattered across Europe or beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T09:01:47-07:00","id":1489417,"title":"","content":"48)Two high-ranking members of the meret\u2019s cults get caught up in gambling debts, and owe a LOT of money. The mob sends people to collect; it gets ugly; both cultists get shot to death. But no money. So, the mob starts looking into the cultists\u2019 associates and, though they know it not, they discover many members of the cult. The mob begins to terrorize the cults.<br /> <br /> They call up the meret, these cults, and now it\u2019s some unfortunate capo going up against a meret fresh on its Descent!<br /> <br /> 49)After defeating another Arisen and claiming the cultists for themselves, they discover the rather strange beliefs this other cult held. Sun worshippers, they identified their mummy as a \u201cBak-Ra\u201d, who in turn took the title from some unworthy demon that sought to slander the sun\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> But the original Bak-Ra has somehow returned. Weakened after millennia bound beneath the earth, this demon shared some similarities with vampires, but <i>doesn\u2019t burn in the sunlight</i>. The original Bak-Ra wants its cult back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-07-2022, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T11:52:05-07:00","id":1489657,"title":"","content":"50)A meret awakens to a Descent where the Vietnam War spilled out of all control, and a non-nuclear WWIII resulting thereby. Supernaturals have been forced out into the open, and thus <i>everything</i> has changed! Asia is engulfed in constant, open conflict and the Arisen are publically known.<br /> <br /> What will the meret do while it\u2019s here? Will they return to the \u2018normal\u2019 timeline upon their next Descent? Or are they stuck here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T20:06:08-07:00","id":1493501,"title":"","content":"Something went badly wrong, and the Mummy's cult vanished. Some college students got hold of some misunderstood lore and successfully summoned the Mummy, believing they were summoning a wish-granting entity.<br /> The Mummy must restore their cult, probably starting with any surviving students who might still want a wish granted.<br /> (Based loosely on &quot;Ow, my sanity&quot;)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T18:28:42-07:00","id":1493793,"title":"","content":"52)Tiny charred monkeys, their flesh cooked and raw and seared, begin to appear in Neter-Khertet. The fiends leave them be, strangely enough, but the monkeys simply will not leave the local Arisen alone. What ARE these damnable things? Wat do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T11:31:24-07:00","id":1493842,"title":"","content":"53)Something huge and swollen with corpse-gas crawls on all fours out of the Underworld into Neter-Khertet, eyes spilling smoke and mouth more lamprey-like than human. It heads towards a nearby hidden trove of relics the PCs\u2019 meret have stashed away, and will single-mindedly seek to gather them up and return to the Underworld, where the Arisen can\u2019t possibly follow.<br /> <br /> Wat do?<br /> <br /> 54)In the ruins of Crocodopolis in Egypt, hidden from the view of tourists and natives alike, in the local Neter-Khertet sit monolithic houses of Amkhata once thought of as gods by the ancients. Scribes and Sekhem sorcerers and psychics made these things, these stitched-together horrors, to imitate the terrible glory of the Judges and the more slothful gods of Duat.<br /> <br /> But Anpu shook with rage at seeing such mockery, and he waged war on these mighty Amkhata, locking them away in spirit-temples made of ephemera, prayer and futile hope.<br /> <br /> Antinous, Attis, Cybele and Serapis and more are names of the things Anpu locked away here. These prison-houses contain valuable relics and vessels, but breaking into them is a fool\u2019s quest. (Strangely, in a way no mummy can explain, werewolves keep randomly popping up in the house-tomb of Serapis. Truly, the will of Anpu is strange and weird and unguessable. Such is the way of gods and monsters indistinguishable from gods.)<br /> <br /> 55)The meret makes a horrifying discovery while hunting relics in the possession of a world-famous museum\u2014-a set of relics from <i>Ki-En-Gir</i>, Irem\u2019s most notorious enemies.<br /> <br /> Memory is clear: Ki-En-Gir magic, while mighty, was not the equal of Utterances, relics and Sekhem sorcery. The Ki-En-Gir city-states did not power itself with Sekhem, but some other, now lost to time mystical energies.<br /> <br /> And yet...the proof is indisputable. This flies in the face of everything Memory teaches the Arisen. Wat do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-27-2022, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T13:48:29-07:00","id":1494551,"title":"","content":"60) Your Judge has given you a commandment; seek out the Relics known as Hero's Mercy, Sleep of Eternal Rest and The Movement of Echoed Dreams, a fairly normal request. There are a few differences and complications though...in addition to not knowing anything else about these Relics, you are told to return these Relics to their Arisen creators and none of these Relics belong to your Guild...or any of the other Major Guilds. (In honour of BoLD's release, I figured throwing some unusual Relic forms and their Minor Guilds at players could be fun. Remember the Judges don't really care the inter-Guild politics, and are more upset with the Temakh of the Shan'aitu than the Arkhem-Urtu themselves. Plus I like the idea that Neoliths, Ankhs and Seba are just as important to the Judges schemes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T13:39:08-07:00","id":1511908,"title":"","content":"61. TE Lawrence, more famously known as Lawrence of Arabia was an archeologist and intelligence agent for the British government against the Ottoman Empire during world war 1. He was also the man who first dubbed the legend of Iram of the pillars the \u201cAtlantis of the Sands\u201d. He also intended to explore Arabia searching for Ubar/Iram (in the real world they are speculated to be the same city), even suggesting using an airship to do so. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s it. That\u2019s the adventure hook. Expedition in a dirigible searching for the cursed city of Ubar in the 1920s. Definitely going to attract the interest of several cults, half want it to fail and half succeed. And of course nothing good is likely to be waiting there for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T08:22:07-07:00","id":1512012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1469515-1001-mummy-2e-plot-hooks?p=1511908#post1511908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely going to attract the interest of several cults, half want it to fail and half succeed. And of course nothing good is likely to be waiting there for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, those cultists/cults who want it to fail are split approx. 33/33//34 between not wanting heathens to disturb a potentially sacred site, wanting to keep whatever Judges-forsaken thing(s) are still in there actually contained, or some other reason entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T15:22:04-07:00","id":1513009,"title":"","content":"62. This idea comes from a conspiracy theory regarding the Great Fire of London in 1666 AD. Freemasonry was, of course, very popular in that city, especially among those with an interest in engineering and design. So logically it makes sense that many of the architects employed to rebuild the city after it was reduced to ashes were a part of that society. But of course the speculation is that this strange society or some more mysterious order using it as a front deployed these men to build the city to their specifications. Some have even gone so far as to claim the city of London has been aligned along a grid pattern that matches such things as the Seal of Solomon or the Kabbalistic Tree of Life. Obviously in the Chronicles of Darkness this can all be perfectly true, and a Mummy Cult or a Meret of Mummies could have pulled the strings of these architects. But I realized this idea isn't confined to London. How many large cities don't have some tragic history of large scale accidents from fires, or earth quakes, or hurricanes, etc? One has to wonder in the Chronicles how many of these disasters weren't actually the work of an Arisen with geomantic ambitions for the city. After all, several Utterances are capable of causing the ground to shatter, or to summon down meteors, or to transform the Deathless into a pillar of fire hotter than the Sun. It would only take a little careful planning, a knowledge of Iremite Geomancy, some carefully recruited architects into the ranks of the cult, and finally one night of destruction followed by a few strings pulled with the recovery efforts and any given city could be realigned to serve the occult needs of a given Mummy or Guild. Of course, a rival mummy could just as easily do something similar to spoil those efforts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T07:23:26-07:00","id":1513071,"title":"","content":"63.) You arise in a caravan in desert not far outside the borders of the Old Empire, with your Sahu able to pass for mortal and at half of the power you would expect upon arising...and you have more of wits about too, come to think of it. What is more, this Descent is mired in a current of time as far from the usual you cannot help feel the flow. The Judges are quieter, but their whispers are full of warning. A city of cold metal and full of foreign faith that weighs heavily upon the land. This is clearly an early departure, long before even the Cannibal Hymn.<br /> There are Vessels here, hidden in unnaturally warped spaces and protected by a strange cold sorcery, a mirror of the red shores within the design. Spirits of iron and belief pose as people here, in service to those design or god who dwells (if they are not the same) abound everywhere, watching the people and guarding the prizes you were sent here to steal away.<br /> And it is indeed theft you were called upon for. Secrecy from this deity is paramount to the Judge's demands.<br /> Where are you? And what does this have to do with the half-breed children of the exiled mechanical spirits of faith?<br /> (Giants in the Earth is heavily inspiring this, but i couldn't resist)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T09:12:10-08:00","id":1527500,"title":"","content":"Comparing notes with your meret and other trusted mummies, you find convincing evidence that <i>some</i> power is capable of hiding relics from your senses; the kepher echo of at least one relic has gone completely silent on the verge of collection, only to be picked up again out of nowhere later on by another mummy.<br /> If you investigate, between your meret and cults you discover a relic that doesn't register to kepher at all.<br /> <br /> The idea being, the Judges actually do have secret uses for relics circulating in the world, and only flag the ones they want back for their mummies to retrieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 12-27-2023, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T12:41:52-07:00","id":1554167,"title":"","content":"65. The meret wakes up to find themselves in a manor at a party. It's the Victorian Era and your meret had the unfortunate luck to be the mummies picked for the party where Victorians liked to show off the contents of the tombs they looted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T12:08:41-08:00","id":1556180,"title":"","content":"Here's one:<br /> A Shuankhsen, made from a slave taken from Ki-en-Gir during its war with Irem, has never lost his faith in the strange and mostly unreachable land of black void and abject unreality his people once worshipped. For millennia, he's sought its power to break his connection to Ammut, but, until recently, has made no real progress.<br /> <br /> That is, until he meets the Deceived known as the Star Pharaoh (as described in <i>Book of the Deceived)</i>. Now, the Shuankhsen js cooking with fire!<br /> <br /> The meret awakening as one, the Judges' words burning in their minds: <i>Crush the twin traitors who seek to call upon Ki-en-Gir!</i>, a purpose built into them by their masters at the start of their collective Descent.<br /> <br /> Here's another:<br /> Valor, Connecticut, USA was a peaceful town full of hardworking folk filled with loving families. A mummy is passing through, when....<i>a benbenet</i> is conjured, and an the avatar of a Judge crawls from forward from a nightmare un-reality of screaming pillars of skulls and skinned celebrants emasculating themselves in ecstatic madness. It proceeds to attack <i>the entire town of Valor</i>, but sparing the mummy.<br /> <br /> What the hell was secretly happening here that prompted <i>THIS</i> level of response from Duat?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28921,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","user":"CreatorFounderMaker","date":". 12-06-2025, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:00:24-08:00","id":1556243,"title":"","content":"Here's one:<br /> [Deceived]<br /> A Bane Seba called <i>the Crown of Wepwawet</i> is discovered by a lone Su-Menent while following Kepher in Uraq's Empty Quarter, but is quickly consumed by the item's foul power, making her one of the few non-Deceived to ever attuned a Seba. Unfortunately, it's a <i>Bane Seba</i>!<br /> <br /> She who wears <i>the Crown of Wepwawet</i> starts gestating a reincarnating Chthonic Being (presumably named Wepwawet). Irregardless of gender, the mummy quickly discovers they are pregnant, and monstrous appetites designed to feed the horrible fetus quickly descends upon them. Memory suffers rapidly, and strange <i>new</i> recollections fill the wearer:<br /> <br /> <i>---there is a land of worms, where soulless gods and almost-gods feast forever, under a red cinder of a dead sun, hunting each other as the last remaining food sources<br /> <br /> ---I am [untranslatable], and I will hunt in this new world of hateful light and vibrant life for it is my nature to be [untranslatable] and ever-hungry<br /> <br /> ---feed me, mother, that i might consume you from within and be born---</i><br /> <br /> Thr PCs Deceived meret defeated the Su-Menent, but were unable to claim the accursed Seba.<br /> <br /> Now, centuries later, <i>the Crown of Wepwawet</i> resurfaced, this time in the hands of a Shuankhsen! Can the PCs' meet successfully capture the hateful star of false inspiration? Or will it escape once more?<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Crown of Wepwawet</i>: Bane Seba</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Ammut has consumed stars, though she she rarely does so now. Some stars house Chthonic Beings, alien to any cosmology known.<br /> <br /> The star Ammut ate, then regurgitated a dead star as <i>the Crown of Wepwawet, which c</i>ontains the broken identity of a single Chthonic Being associated with said devoured star, a horror that must take new flesh by impregnatinvg itself into the <i>Crown</i>'s new wearer.<br /> <br /> 9 weeks later, a terrible thing of stardust and whirling gyre maws and a vaguely trilobite outline tears itself free from within the wearer, artifically ending their Descent and attaining a state of Twilight.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b><br /> [/b]The pregnancy is immediately initiated by the Deceived sacrificing a single level of Bashing damage.<br /> The pregnancy last nine weeks. At the end of every werk, the mummy must suffer yet more damage:<br /> \u25cf Week 1-3: Each week, one level of Bashing damage.<br /> \u25cf Week 4-6: Each week, convert one of these Bashing levels of damage to Lethal.<br /> \u25cf Week 7-8: Gain one level of Aggravated damage per week.<br /> \u25cf Due date: The Chthonic Beingvis birthed, bloodily erupting into Twilight as an aberrant fetal horror.<br /> <br /> Gimme some time to think about it; I'll get back to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28921,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","user":"CreatorFounderMaker","date":". 12-07-2025, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T14:01:58-08:00","id":1556313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1469515-1001-mummy-2e-plot-hooks?p=1513071#post1513071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">63.) You arise in a caravan in desert not far outside the borders of the Old Empire, with your Sahu able to pass for mortal and at half of the power you would expect upon arising...and you have more of wits about too, come to think of it. What is more, this Descent is mired in a current of time as far from the usual you cannot help feel the flow. The Judges are quieter, but their whispers are full of warning. A city of cold metal and full of foreign faith that weighs heavily upon the land. This is clearly an early departure, long before even the Cannibal Hymn.<br /> There are Vessels here, hidden in unnaturally warped spaces and protected by a strange cold sorcery, a mirror of the red shores within the design. Spirits of iron and belief pose as people here, in service to those design or god who dwells (if they are not the same) abound everywhere, watching the people and guarding the prizes you were sent here to steal away.<br /> And it is indeed theft you were called upon for. Secrecy from this deity is paramount to the Judge's demands.<br /> Where are you? And what does this have to do with the half-breed children of the exiled mechanical spirits of faith?<br /> (Giants in the Earth is heavily inspiring this, but i couldn't resist)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this. <i>Demon: The Descent</i> has little reason to do crossover with <i>Mummy: The Curse</i>, so this is a neat treat to read.!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T23:26:25-08:00","id":1556333,"title":"","content":"69). An Immortal has reached out to your meret because some sort local cult has performed sorcery that they don't recognise and it has altered both the flow of occult energies and the memories of the local mortals. Even if you turn them away, you soon find that the Immortal wasn't wrong about the changes.<br /> Kepher is more difficult to use, tomb geometries do not flow as they once did and even your cult/s do not hold even to the teachings of your Judge, as if you swore your decree to something else.<br /> <br /> When you investigate either this local cult or the sorcery, you find they are, in way, one and the same. By acting against this distribution, parts of local this foreign magic extract themselves into some sort of automaton spirits to strike back.<br /> <br /> (I do like finding places where I can leverage the overlap between the gamelines. I haven't even got to actual Unchained yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:22:59-08:00","id":1556364,"title":"","content":"Oo! God-Machine cults and angels vs the Arisen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:24:40-08:00","id":1556390,"title":"","content":"Here's one:<br /> The Red Shore of Nu, while known tknowe Arisen, are generally a mystery they are none too eager to solve. It a strange, alien place for the last inheritors of the Nameless Empire.<br /> <br /> So, when a cult worshipping Ra begins secretly showing <i>real</i> occult might, the PCs' meret investigates. Expecting to find a mummy at this new cult's heart, the meret finds that the Nameless Falcon has a <i>very</i> DIFFERENT manifestation in the Red Shore of Nu, that of an Apocalyptic incarnation of wrath, truth and impervious arrogance.<br /> <br /> This new cult has summoned a minion of the sun-god, preparing via complex rituals for the solar spirit to Claim a falcon bred for five generations to host such holy power.<br /> <br /> what does the meret do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}